  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial release: shared Docker building blocks, and a declared source model for getting an application into a container.\nWorth knowing up front:\n- Where a container's application comes from is declared, not guessed: Image(...), Project(...) - resolved against the file that declares it - or Directory(...). Project facts come from MSBuild rather than from inspecting paths, a multi-targeted project is a hard error instead of a silent pick, and the whole resolved plan is logged before anything is built, so a failure can be read against what was going to happen.\n- Published ports bind to 127.0.0.1, not to every interface. A test SQL Server or emulator is no longer reachable from the rest of the network while a suite runs. Set TESTFRAMEWORK_CONTAINER_HOST_IP when the Docker daemon is remote and the loopback default would make the port unreachable.\n- Docker host detection runs before the first connection. Docker Desktop on Windows exposes the engine under more than one named pipe, and picking the wrong one produced a connection failure on a machine where Docker was working fine.\n- Images and temporary build output this package creates are labelled and swept when they are more than a day old, because a killed test host leaves them behind and the container reaper does not cover them. Set TESTFRAMEWORK_CONTAINER_NO_SWEEP to disable.\n- Docker CLI invocations are bounded by a timeout, so a wedged CLI fails teardown instead of hanging it forever.",
